# Relay desktop UI catalog, English (en), section: Background (stay available with no window, call alert, answer automatically). Same ids and $variables as localizations/en/background.ftl. See docs/i18n.md.

background-label = Stay available in the background
background-help = Keeps Relay reachable and ringing while the window or app is closed, as long as this device is on the network.
background-battery-warning = Battery optimization may stop Relay from ringing while the app is closed.
background-battery-button = Allow in battery settings
background-notifications-warning = Notifications are off, so you would not see incoming calls while the app is closed.
background-notifications-button = Allow notifications
alert-title = Call alert
alert-help = How an incoming call gets your attention.
alert-system-device = Follow device settings
alert-system-desktop = Follow system settings
alert-ring-vibrate = Ring and vibrate
alert-ring = Ring
alert-vibrate = Vibrate only
alert-silent = Silent
auto-answer-global = Allow automatic answering
auto-answer-global-help = When off, nobody is answered automatically, even contacts set up for it. Your choices per contact are kept.
contact-auto-answer = Answer automatically
contact-auto-answer-unverified = Verify this device first
contact-auto-answer-badge = Answers automatically
auto-answer-ask = { $name } will be able to call you and be answered without you touching the device, opening your microphone as set under "{ $mode }". Only do this for people you trust.
auto-answer-yes = Yes, answer automatically
call-auto-answered = Answered automatically
err-auto-answer-verified = Only verified contacts can answer automatically. Compare the safety code on both devices first.
